{
  "slug": "essentials/components",
  "title": "Building with Components",
  "description": "Components are the fundamental building blocks of Angular applications, combining TypeScript logic, HTML templates, and CSS styling.",
  "source": "https://angular.dev/essentials/components",
  "status": "reviewed",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In Angular, a component encapsulates the structure, styling, and behavior of a piece of UI. Every component is defined as a TypeScript class adorned with the `@Component` decorator."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "create-component",
      "text": "Creating a Component"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Here is an example of defining a simple standalone component to display a user avatar photo:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "profile-photo.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import { Component } from '@angular/core';",
        "",
        "@Component({",
        "  selector: 'profile-photo',",
        "  standalone: true,",
        "  template: `",
        "    <div class=\"photo-card\">",
        "      <img src=\"profile.jpg\" alt=\"Profile photo\" />",
        "    </div>",
        "  `,",
        "  styles: [`",
        "    .photo-card { border-radius: 50%; overflow: hidden; }",
        "  `]",
        "})",
        "export class ProfilePhoto {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "text": "Components should adhere to the Single Responsibility Principle. If a template grows too large, extract child components to keep code clean and maintainable."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "use-component",
      "text": "Using Components inside other Components"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "With Standalone Components, simply import the child component in the `imports` array of the parent:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "user-profile.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import { Component } from '@angular/core';",
        "import { ProfilePhoto } from './profile-photo.component';",
        "",
        "@Component({",
        "  selector: 'user-profile',",
        "  standalone: true,",
        "  imports: [ProfilePhoto],",
        "  template: `",
        "    <section class=\"profile-container\">",
        "      <profile-photo />",
        "      <h2>Jane Doe</h2>",
        "      <p>Angular Software Engineer</p>",
        "    </section>",
        "  `",
        "})",
        "export class UserProfile {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "inputs-and-outputs",
      "text": "Passing data with Signal Inputs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Declare reactive input properties using the modern `input()` function:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "user-badge.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import { Component, input } from '@angular/core';",
        "",
        "@Component({",
        "  selector: 'user-badge',",
        "  standalone: true,",
        "  template: `<span class=\"badge\">{{ username() }}</span>`",
        "})",
        "export class UserBadge {",
        "  username = input.required<string>();",
        "}"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
